From 4c65699d12d06a64206cecff620e1eab6a190192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:03:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] uhf: retry the transport connection on openSession(),
 and fix dumpsys's semantics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two real gaps, reported from actual hardware testing:

1. Reader presence was latched at boot. A UART reader has no uevent to
   re-probe on, unlike a hot-pluggable USB device — if it was absent or
   unpowered when performStartupReset() ran once at boot,
   transport.isOpen() stays false forever; nothing ever tried again, not
   a HAL restart, not openSession(), which just checked/set exclusivity
   and never touched the transport at all. Only a reboot recovered it.

   openSession() now retries performStartupReset() when the transport
   isn't open, exactly once per absence (transport.isOpen() becomes true
   regardless of whether the reader actually answers - see point 2 -
   so this doesn't retry on every single call). Best-effort, not gating:
   the session is still granted even if the retry's own transact() also
   times out, the same way a reader that disappears mid-session doesn't
   retroactively invalidate the session already open. openSession()
   arbitrates exclusivity (FR-LC-03), not hardware presence (FR-LC-01);
   the caller's own next call surfaces the real error, same as always.

2. dumpsys uhf conflated "open() succeeded" with "a reply arrived":
   it reported "transport open (reader responded to startup reset):
   true" while rx had been 0 since boot, because opening a UART fd
   always succeeds as soon as the device node exists, whether or not
   anything is actually attached and answering on the other end -
   exactly the failure this diagnostic exists to surface, hidden by its
   own wrong label.

   Added UhfSessionArbiter#hasReaderResponded(), tracking whether a
   transact() has actually completed since the transport was last
   (re)opened - set true only when performStartupReset()'s own
   transact() doesn't throw, reset to false at the start of every
   attempt. UhfService#dump() now reports transport-open and
   reader-responded as two separate lines instead of one conflated one,
   and "reader connected" now reflects hasReaderResponded(), not
   isTransportOpen().

Verified by actually compiling and running the full UhfSessionArbiterTest
suite (68 tests, up from 63) with real javac + JUnit 4. Three existing
tests (setEnabledAntennas_skipsTheInterlockWhenCheckWasAlreadyOff,
killTag_rejectsAllZeroPassword,
lockTag_permanentStateWithoutConfirmIsRejected) called openSession()
against a never-opened FakeTransport and asserted an exact/empty call
log - a real, expected interaction with fix #1's new retry behavior,
not a false positive: updated them to open the transport first (matching
the realistic "already booted" precondition they were actually meant to
test), which is what a real run caught immediately. FakeTransport gained
a one-shot failNextTransact flag to let the new tests simulate "fd opened
fine, reader didn't reply" - the exact real bug being fixed - as
distinct from "transport never opened at all".

UhfService.java itself isn't host-compilable (real Android framework
dependencies), so the dump() change there was verified by careful
inline review only, not execution - noted here rather than glossed over.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../com/android/server/uhf/UhfService.java    | 16 +++-
 .../android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiter.java | 31 +++++++
 .../server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiterTest.java     | 84 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 128 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfService.java
index 23a90fc9..acefab4f 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfService.java
@@ -663,15 +663,25 @@ public final class UhfService extends SystemService {
                 return;
             }
             boolean transportOpen = mArbiter.isTransportOpen();
+            boolean readerResponded = mArbiter.hasReaderResponded();
             pw.println("UhfService:");
-            pw.println("  transport open (reader responded to startup reset): " + transportOpen);
+            // Two separate lines on purpose, not one: transportOpen only means the HAL's fd is
+            // valid, which for a UART is true as soon as the device node exists, whether or not
+            // anything is attached to the far end — it was previously mislabeled here as "reader
+            // responded to startup reset", which is readerResponded's job, not transportOpen's.
+            pw.println("  transport open (device node fd valid): " + transportOpen);
+            pw.println("  reader responded (answered at least one command since last (re)open): "
+                    + readerResponded);
             // Kept in sync by hand with hardware/rockchip/uhf/aidl/default/UhfReader.cpp's
             // kDevicePathProperty — system_server has no other way to know which node the HAL
             // opened, short of adding AIDL surface purely for this diagnostic, which isn't worth
-            // it for a value already visible via getprop.
+            // it for a value already visible via getprop. Needs its own get_prop(system_server,
+            // uhf_prop) sepolicy grant to actually see the configured value rather than silently
+            // falling back to the default here too — see hal_uhf.te's own comment on why a plain
+            // vendor_default_prop grant can't cover this on this tree.
             pw.println("  configured device (ro.vendor.uhf.device, HAL default /dev/ttyUSB0): "
                     + SystemProperties.get("ro.vendor.uhf.device", "/dev/ttyUSB0"));
-            pw.println("  reader connected: " + (transportOpen ? "yes" : "no"));
+            pw.println("  reader connected: " + (readerResponded ? "yes" : "no"));
             pw.println("  open sessions: " + mSessions.size());
         }
     }
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiter.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiter.java
index 464d8c08..9dd2d6ef 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiter.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiter.java
@@ -122,6 +122,11 @@ public final class UhfSessionArbiter {
     public static final int LOCK_PERM_LOCKED = 3; // LOCK_* constants — see UhfService's mapping.
 
     private Object holder; // null = no session held
+    // Distinct from transport.isOpen(): opening a UART fd always succeeds as soon as the device
+    // node exists, whether or not anything is actually attached to the far end — it says nothing
+    // about whether the reader has ever answered. Set only by a transact() inside
+    // performStartupReset() actually completing; see hasReaderResponded().
+    private boolean readerResponded;
     private ReaderMode mode = ReaderMode.IDLE;
     private int antennaMask;
     private int rfPower;
@@ -163,10 +168,12 @@ public final class UhfSessionArbiter {
      */
     public synchronized void performStartupReset() throws UhfTransportException {
         transport.open();
+        readerResponded = false; // reset before attempting — see hasReaderResponded()'s doc
         // FR-LC-05: unconditional — do not check current mode first, because a device that was
         // streaming when powered off answers this exact query with more streamed tag frames, not
         // a clean answer. Force the transition every time.
         transport.transact(CMD_REALTIME_MODE, new byte[] {0x00}, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS);
+        readerResponded = true; // only reached if the transact above didn't throw
         mode = ReaderMode.IDLE;
 
         // FR-LC-09: region is reasserted from platform storage, not read back and trusted. If the
@@ -188,9 +195,33 @@ public final class UhfSessionArbiter {
         if (holder != null) {
             throw new UhfBusyException();
         }
+        if (!transport.isOpen()) {
+            // A UART reader has no uevent to re-probe on, unlike a hot-pluggable USB device: if
+            // it was absent or unpowered when performStartupReset() ran at boot, nothing else
+            // ever retries until this exact moment — a client actually asking to use it. Only
+            // reachable once per absence: transport.isOpen() is true after this regardless of
+            // whether the reader actually answered (see hasReaderResponded()), so a session that
+            // opens against a still-absent reader gets exactly one retry here, not one per call.
+            //
+            // Best-effort, not gating: still grant the session even if this fails, the same way
+            // a reader that disappears mid-session doesn't retroactively invalidate the session
+            // that was already open — openSession() arbitrates exclusivity (FR-LC-03), not
+            // hardware presence (FR-LC-01); the caller's own next call surfaces the real error.
+            try {
+                performStartupReset();
+            } catch (UhfTransportException ignored) {
+            }
+        }
         holder = clientToken;
     }
 
+    /** Distinct from {@link #isTransportOpen}: whether the reader has actually answered at least
+     * one command since the transport was last (re)opened, not just whether the fd is valid —
+     * opening a UART succeeds regardless of whether anything is attached to the far end. */
+    public synchronized boolean hasReaderResponded() {
+        return readerResponded;
+    }
+
     /** Graceful close, called by the client itself. */
     public synchronized void closeSession(Object clientToken) {
         requireHolder(clientToken);
diff --git a/services/tests/servicestests/src/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiterTest.java b/services/tests/servicestests/src/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiterTest.java
index 82948923..30ceb898 100644
--- a/services/tests/servicestests/src/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiterTest.java
+++ b/services/tests/servicestests/src/com/android/server/uhf/UhfSessionArbiterTest.java
@@ -113,6 +113,70 @@ public class UhfSessionArbiterTest {
         assertTrue(arbiter.isHeldBy(clientB));
     }
 
+    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+    // A UART reader has no uevent to re-probe on: if it was absent/unpowered at boot,
+    // performStartupReset() never gets a second chance until a client actually asks to use it.
+    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+    @Test
+    public void openSession_retriesStartupResetWhenTransportWasNeverOpened() throws Exception {
+        Object client = new Object();
+        assertFalse("precondition: nothing has opened the transport yet", transport.isOpen());
+
+        arbiter.openSession(client);
+
+        assertTrue("openSession() must retry the boot-time reset it never got",
+                transport.calls.contains("open"));
+        assertTrue(transport.isOpen());
+        assertTrue(arbiter.isHeldBy(client));
+    }
+
+    @Test
+    public void openSession_grantsTheSessionEvenWhenTheRetryStillFindsNoReader() throws Exception {
+        Object client = new Object();
+        transport.failNextTransact = true; // the retry's own transact() times out too
+
+        arbiter.openSession(client); // must not throw — exclusivity, not hardware presence
+
+        assertTrue("session grant is best-effort on the retry, not gated by its success",
+                arbiter.isHeldBy(client));
+    }
+
+    @Test
+    public void openSession_doesNotRetryWhenTransportIsAlreadyOpen() throws Exception {
+        Object client = new Object();
+        arbiter.performStartupReset();
+        transport.reset();
+
+        arbiter.openSession(client);
+
+        assertTrue("no reason to redo the reset sequence when the transport never closed",
+                transport.calls.isEmpty());
+    }
+
+    @Test
+    public void hasReaderResponded_isFalseUntilATransactActuallySucceeds() throws Exception {
+        transport.failNextTransact = true;
+        try {
+            arbiter.performStartupReset();
+            fail("expected the injected timeout to propagate");
+        } catch (UhfTransportException expected) {
+            // pass
+        }
+
+        assertTrue("fd is open regardless of whether the reader ever replied",
+                transport.isOpen());
+        assertFalse("no reply was actually received — must not be conflated with isOpen()",
+                arbiter.hasReaderResponded());
+    }
+
+    @Test
+    public void hasReaderResponded_isTrueOnceStartupResetActuallyGetsAReply() throws Exception {
+        arbiter.performStartupReset();
+
+        assertTrue(arbiter.hasReaderResponded());
+    }
+
     @Test
     public void onClientDied_releasesSessionAndReturnsReaderToIdle() throws Exception {
         Object clientA = new Object();
@@ -210,6 +274,10 @@ public class UhfSessionArbiterTest {
     @Test
     public void setEnabledAntennas_skipsTheInterlockWhenCheckWasAlreadyOff() throws Exception {
         Object client = new Object();
